### Start Infrastructure
# Run this in your terminal first:
# docker-compose up -d
# ./mvnw spring-boot:run

### 1. Test Places Autocomplete
GET http://localhost:8080/api/places/autocomplete?input=Koramangala&lat=12.9904909&lng=77.6702519
Accept: application/json

### 2. Test Reverse Geocoding
GET http://localhost:8080/api/places/reverse-geocode?lat=12.9904909&lng=77.6702519
Accept: application/json

### 3. Mark a Driver as Available
# First we need to tell Redis that a driver is online and ready for orders
POST http://localhost:8080/api/fleet/availability
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cityId": "BENGALURU",
  "driverId": "driver-123",
  "available": true
}

### 4. Dispatch an Order
# This will try to find the nearest driver in a 5km radius to the restaurant coords
# NOTE: This requires driver telemetry to be in Redis first (via WebSockets or manual Redis insertion)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/logistics/dispatch
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cityId": "BENGALURU",
  "restaurantCoords": "12.934533,77.626579"
}

### 5. Turn-by-Turn Routing (Directions API)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/logistics/route?origin=12.934533,77.626579&destination=12.9715987,77.5945627
Accept: application/json

### 6. Test Model Context Protocol (MCP) Server SSE Endpoint
# This endpoint is what LLMs and AI Agents connect to
GET http://localhost:8080/mcp/sse
Accept: text/event-stream

### 7. Get All Available Drivers
GET http://localhost:8080/api/fleet/available?cityId=BENGALURU
Accept: application/json

### 8. Update Driver Location (Simulate a driver near the restaurant)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/fleet/location
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cityId": "BENGALURU",
  "driverId": "driver-123",
  "lat": 12.935000,
  "lng": 77.625000
}

### 9. Get Top 10 Nearby Drivers
GET http://localhost:8080/api/fleet/nearby?cityId=BENGALURU&lat=12.934533&lng=77.626579&radius=5.0
Accept: application/json

### 10. Get Specific Driver Location
GET http://localhost:8080/api/fleet/location?cityId=BENGALURU&driverId=driver-123
Accept: application/json

### 11. Delete a Driver (Simulate driver going offline permanently)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/fleet/driver?cityId=BENGALURU&driverId=driver-123
Accept: application/json
